 = (switch_diff * logit_q - log_regular_diff)','score_diff = (switch_diff * logit_q[participant_id] - log_regular_diff)')\ndoc_old=src.split('\"\"\"')[1]\nsrc=src.replace(doc_old,'''Person-specific belief about how often a fair coin switches.\n\nRefinement of `length_normalised_chance_vs_motif`. A sequence looks random to\nthe extent the person's model of a fair coin (switching with probability q)\nexplains it better than the regular generators (Markov coin, biased coin,\nrepeating motif with slips; unknowns integrated out), the log evidence\ndifference weighed per flip by a fitted power of length, with person-specific\ndecision sensitivity. Single change: q -- the one distortion of the normative\nchance model -- is person-specific, drawn from a population on the logit\nscale, so some people may believe chance is streaky (q < 1/2) and prefer\nsequences with fewer switches while most believe it over-alternates.\n''',1)\nopen('iter_0/candidate_0/candidate.py','w').write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_0 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3442,"cache_read_input_tokens":56862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3442,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0b3f086-270b-4edd-a254-abbbcabae6fb","uuid":"41b5710f-16ee-4033-b165-35a